The '''sulfur caves''' is a cave [[biome]] composed of [[sulfur]] and [[cinnabar]] blocks, where [[sulfur cube]]s and [[cave spider]]s spawn. [[Sulfur pool]]s with [[potent sulfur]] generate here, in addition to [[sulfur spike]]s.

== Generation ==
Sulfur caves generate underground at the same depth as [[lush caves]] and [[dripstone caves]], although it is much smaller in size and more fragmented. [[Sulfur spring]]s sometimes generate at the surface, indicating there are sulfur caves below.

The biome generates only at low [[weirdness]] values (≤ -0.45). This means that it commonly borders any other cave biome, and above-ground are usually [[mountains]] or plateaus, and never generates close to [[river]]s, although it can generate under the [[ocean]]. However, if sulfur caves generate at higher erosion, there may also be more middle biomes, [[desert]] biomes, and shattered biomes.

Rarely, sulfur caves can generate above ground at weirdness values above 1.0, which occurs inside mountain rings.

== Description ==
The main landscape is composed of [[sulfur]] and [[cinnabar]] layers in approximately same amount of blocks, with frequent [[sulfur pool]]s possessing a unique acid-green color of [[water]]. [[Potent sulfur]] is found only on the bottom of these pools, creating noxious gas with white bubbles particles in and on top of the water. [[Nausea]] is inflicted to mobs and players when they come in contact with this noxious gas. The gas can be removed by destroying the [[potent sulfur]] under the water.

Other terrain blocks such as [[deepslate]] and [[stone]] variants generate between the sulfur and cinnabar, and [[glow lichen]] is noticeably more common.{{Only|be|short=1}}

[[Ores]] rarely generate here, because sulfur and cinnabar replace most stone and deepslate blocks.

